    <param.company>Warsaw University of Technology</param.company>
    <param.summary>Seismic signal polarimetric analysis application for research and educational purposes.</param.summary>
    <param.description>This application is designed for research and teaching in the field of seismic signal analysis and wave polarization. It allows users to load three-component seismic recordings, perform signal decimation and preprocessing, and compute time–frequency representations using STFT. The tool further derives and visualizes Stokes parameters (S0–S3) for polarimetric analysis, supporting both Rayleigh and Love wave modes. Additional features include adjustable interpolation methods, colormap selection, saturation control, and interactive time/frequency domain visualization.</param.description>
